WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.353
AI-assisted assessment depends on evidence
quality.

2
00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:13.812
Useful source material can include asset
inventories, IAM exports,

3
00:00:13.892 --> 00:00:21.653
configuration snapshots, cloud posture
findings, logging summaries,

4
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:28.857
architecture diagrams,
infrastructure-as-code, tagging data,

5
00:00:28.937 --> 00:00:37.462
security group and firewall summaries,
storage permissions, workload lists,

6
00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:43.776
and vulnerability scan summaries from
authorized tools.

7
00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:50.472
Each source contributes a different view
of the environment.

8
00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:57.549
Asset and IAM exports help answer what
exists and who can reach it.

9
00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:04.754
Configuration snapshots reveal how
services are actually set up.

10
00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:12.977
Infrastructure-as-code can show intended
state and deployment patterns.

11
00:01:13.057 --> 00:01:18.146
Architecture diagrams explain design
intent,

12
00:01:18.226 --> 00:01:24.715
while logs and telemetry summaries show
observed activity.

13
00:01:24.795 --> 00:01:30.138
Posture findings can highlight candidate
risks,

14
00:01:30.218 --> 00:01:34.926
but they still need validation and
context.

15
00:01:35.006 --> 00:01:42.512
Provenance matters because a cloud
assessment should be reviewable.

16
00:01:42.592 --> 00:01:47.427
If a report says a storage location is
public,

17
00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:55.140
a reviewer should be able to trace that
claim to a configuration export,

18
00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:02.345
posture finding, command output, ticket,
or owner confirmation.

19
00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:10.822
Without provenance, findings become harder
to trust and harder to remediate.

20
00:02:10.902 --> 00:02:15.101
Evidence should be prepared for AI use.

21
00:02:15.181 --> 00:02:22.814
Remove secrets where possible, minimize
unnecessary sensitive data,

22
00:02:22.894 --> 00:02:30.401
label the source and date of each file,
and keep context about account,

23
00:02:30.481 --> 00:02:33.534
region, service, and owner.

24
00:02:33.614 --> 00:02:37.304
If the evidence is partial, say so.

25
00:02:37.384 --> 00:02:46.545
AI performs better when it knows the
difference between current production exports,

26
00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:52.223
example snippets, old diagrams, and
working notes.

27
00:02:52.303 --> 00:02:58.664
The model should be instructed not to
invent missing facts.

28
00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:05.742
Missing owners, unclear identities,
unknown data sensitivity,

29
00:03:05.822 --> 00:03:12.565
or incomplete logging evidence should
become open questions.

30
00:03:12.645 --> 00:03:20.660
This keeps the assessment honest and gives
the team a clear follow-up path.
